36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"T2","old":"60–150s, ask 47–58¢, BRTI move ≥2bp, 10-minute trend ≥4bp, $5","new":"60–150s, ask 45–60¢, BRTI move ≥2bp, 10-minute trend ≥3bp, $5","reason":"Zero settled trades after ~9 hours. The 47–58¢ / 4bp-trend cousin almost never lined up live (T’s overlapping fill was 59¢ with a −2.5bp trend, which T2 would reject). Widening the ask to T’s 45–60¢ band and easing the trend floor from 4bp to 3bp is the smallest relaxation that stays clearly profitable on the 18-day first-hit backtest (~19 trades/day, +$58 after fees vs the original 13/day and +$130). The suggested 45–180s + 45–60¢ + 3bp combo backtested negative (−$61) and was not used. Time window and the 2bp BRTI-move threshold are unchanged."},{"time_pt":"6:36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"LFC","old":"A’s late favorite (ask ≥0.80, ≤50s left) + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 90s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","new":"A’s late favorite (ask ≥0.80) allowed from ≤70s left + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 60s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","reason":"The 90s confirm was not the main live blocker (0 filter_blocks; two late favorites held ~89s but could not fill into a one-sided late book). Shortening the confirm to 60s eases that filter. Allowing the same ≥0.80 late-favorite price rule from 70s left (instead of 50s) aims to lift an ask before the late book goes one-sided. A 1-minute backtest of slightly earlier late entries stayed strongly positive; a looser 120s-left proxy was still positive but weaker, so the late gate stops at 70s. Hard stop and sizing are unchanged. A’s own 50s late-favorite rule is unchanged."},{"time_pt":"6:36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"M5","old":"T’s 60–150s / 45–60¢ rule, plus 3 consecutive polls where book imbalance I is strictly on the same side (I>0 for UP, I<0 for DOWN), $5","new":"Same T entry rule, plus 2 consecutive polls where I > −0.25 for UP or I < +0.25 for DOWN, $5","reason":"Zero trades in ~26 hours even though T filled three times in that spa